# roastery — node settings. setup-secrets.sh copies this to .env.local
# (gitignored) and asks for anything still REPLACE_ME.
#
# Unlike the Debian fleet nodes, roastery has no /opt/purrbrews/.env from
# init/purrbrews-init.sh (it isn't provisioned by that script) and no
# $DATA_DIR convention -- this is the first app built here, and inventing
# fleet-wide policy off one app's needs isn't worth it yet. compose.sh loads
# this file, then the app's own secrets.env.local if it has one.

TZ=Asia/Kolkata

# Native Windows Traefik -> localhost Ollama, protected by percolator Authelia.
DOMAIN=REPLACE_ME.example.com
LAN_CIDR=192.168.0.0/24
PERCOLATOR_LAN_IP=REPLACE_ME
TRAEFIK_ACME_EMAIL=REPLACE_ME@example.com

# ── immich-ml ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No settings needed yet -- immich-ml has no secrets and no config template.
# One reminder, not a variable (nothing in this repo reads env vars for image
# tags): before bumping immich-ml/docker-compose.yml's image tag, check
# stacks/percolator/immich/docker-compose.yml's immich-server tag first.
# The two must always match -- Immich's own compatibility rule.

# ── Komodo Periphery ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Added 2026-09-16, best-effort on Windows/Docker Desktop -- see
# komodo-periphery/docker-compose.yml's own header comment for what is and
# isn't verified. No scrutiny-collector here: Scrutiny's collector needs
# smartctl access to raw physical disks (SYS_RAWIO/SYS_ADMIN + /dev/sdX or
# /dev/nvmeX passed straight into the container), which Docker Desktop's
# WSL2 VM does not expose the way a native Linux host does -- there is no
# reliable path from a Windows physical disk to a Linux container's
# smartctl without extra host-side tooling this repo doesn't have yet.
# Revisit if that ever changes; not attempted here.
CELLAR_LAN_IP=REPLACE_ME
# One-time bootstrap credential (CONFIRMED 2026-09-17) -- generate from
# cellar's Komodo UI (Settings -> the Servers/onboarding section), matching
# server name "roastery". Needed for first connect only -- core.pub alone
# isn't enough to register this node as a Server. Safe to leave REPLACE_ME
# once roastery shows up as a Server in Komodo's UI.
PERIPHERY_ONBOARDING_KEY=REPLACE_ME
# Unlike every other node, this key is NOT templated through .env.local --
# multi-line PEM content doesn't round-trip cleanly through
# setup-secrets.ps1's single-line ${VAR} substitution (see that script's
# own .template rendering loop; it has no \n-unescaping step the way
# percolator's bash generate-secrets.sh does for AUTHELIA_OIDC_JWK_PRIVATE_KEY).
# Simpler and less error-prone here: copy cellar's
# /srv/data/komodo/keys/core.pub by hand straight into
# komodo-periphery\keys\core.pub on roastery (create the keys\ folder if
# it doesn't exist yet) -- no REPLACE_ME/prompt/template involved for this
# one file.
